{"name":"Cape Palliser","hex":"#75482f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape Palliser / Mātakitaki-a-Kupe","blocks":[{"text":"Cape Palliser / Mātakitaki-a-Kupe is a promontory on the southern coast of New Zealand's North Island and is the southernmost point of the North Island; it is in fact considerably farther south than Nelson or Blenheim in the South Island."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Cape_Palliser.jpg/330px-Cape_Palliser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Palliser_%2F_M%C4%81takitaki-a-Kupe","wikidata":"Q914119"},{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape","wikidata":"Q1034198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg/500px-Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg/1280px-Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg/500px-Seal_at_Cape_Palliser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi